cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CIRN in your research, please cite the software using these metadata."
type: software
title: "Classification-Based Inference of Regulatory Networks (CIRN)"
abstract: >-
  CIRN is an R-based framework for generating directed, signed, temporally
  ordered, and uncertainty-aware regulatory hypotheses from single or
  multivariate time-series data using Bayesian logistic regression with
  lagged state, first-derivative, and second-derivative predictor
  representations.
